{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_07cfa57fc6c9a1515ef4ed7bb048d6400d32f6afd273fd5629568d660376234e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f58e8c78c60adf70baaba9bf2308ed0a9b27d49504c237f36317cad4caa500ea"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"TableChatAgent accepts a dataset (file path, URL, or dataframe) and answers queries by having its LLM generate Pandas code via function-calling, which the agent's handler method executes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3191dcf4143f79c4fb19ea234222695139f58cf52755d67df8f048376c2b19bc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_736bfd374959588c6a44feb9c27243ca4659256e434b6ea4b9e433ad2e555f6f","slc_f6ed399752416a7986efd113e5fd14280156870e3bdd8bf35a43fe5ea57cbf16"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"The multi-agent paradigm is inspired by the Actor model, and the framework does not use LangChain or any other LLM framework, aiming to work with practically any LLM.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3e52077b2ff559f444cf17922e622a22f36aeb92e4fad3c7aad1473fd83d4472","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e812365bd8a81d93d315f6fc64952c1f0bee57cc942b4d8e97e69f3051be5c4","slc_d8981a29230065c0f092c06dbbc2a4e2abc719e80a9285e709b517a33f632ab2"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"LLM configuration supports OpenAI models, any model behind an OpenAI-compatible API (e.g. \"ollama/mistral\"), and local models via chat_model strings such as \"local/localhost:8000\".","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3ec032ee593f0791bdc1b2469a1b5fa0d82c4459385576b8462ec324a22263c5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_09776f22241a49978d5483498ad132d1cc47a4851fa804d12f5c61880a420fc7","slc_0eb7d420f67621d99b23a67dea6e1671ab46970206e4de104bcacbc617bce45e"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"A Claude Code plugin provides two skills: langroid:patterns for generating Langroid multi-agent code using proper design patterns, and langroid:add-pattern for recording newly learned patterns for future reference.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4ecd45cf5e980d9619f4da4a10d9a286eb069c826ba5feb85edbf7d2726aa029","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_261a81012f9db01fd2ce5c58697aa0974f279f69b452391379eace243bd45d46"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"Supported vector stores include Qdrant cloud, Chroma (local storage, no API key needed), LanceDB, and Milvus; Milvus defaults to local storage at ./milvus.db, and Milvus Lite is unavailable on Windows.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_63e23efd773529940518f1fb1ce334167c0f19ea98a08093c016937cdda4a626","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_736bfd374959588c6a44feb9c27243ca4659256e434b6ea4b9e433ad2e555f6f"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"Langroid is a Python framework for building LLM applications where users set up Agents equipped with optional components (LLM, vector-store, tools/functions) that collaborate by exchanging messages.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6ef3ce00978788541270b7a15de8d3f87b6d107643f1ed25178f001d2b6e9c23","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_24722645d653f6fa15a05a275bd938a13ecd2ecb943efbb79bb37fac6f966ec3","slc_d8d34368ba95c835dbaf5c36dffbcf8c777e12db0435f599fa58144127509b1d"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"DocChatAgent supports chat with documents by sharding, embedding, storing in a vector DB, and retrieval-augmented answer generation, configured via DocChatAgentConfig with doc_paths and a vecdb setting.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_73ab4c005b47f9449826fc998b23b84346f099d698f87957cbe10bc2766a1e9d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2786d16fa10435f757dc126e92fbbe729483e3ed182262d7dee1e8cd5b22a5a3"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"The README states the prompts and instructions have been tested to work well with GPT-4 (and to some extent GPT-4o); other LLMs may yield inferior results unless prompts or the multi-agent setup are adjusted.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_80fdc521582a18fe7e7fdd580f8894a842527d41b76ecb654c9c982dcd58771a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6b92c9d22fcdd7580e73cf93b41cb93220f7c9e5a19cf64072f1592d1edb6b93","slc_938ef641df0120eee70eb4f06fb29135bcdcf45d496cab25ceaa30d18cc60055","slc_cee29964b57577c43bf818c59c77b7770a6a6a7aa442f154a3b7c000002cbc6e"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"Tools are defined by subclassing ToolMessage with a request field naming the handling agent method, a purpose description, and typed arguments; agents enable tools via enable_message, and Pydantic validation errors are sent back to the LLM for self-correction.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_82a9b318f87f6bab08b904e3ceddbf455d44f7628120e764f98a211bcb9096a2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_44f4100f9a4e8b8b53d9ddd56b164674fe8ff9b400ce6798b2eb2a7bc518988b"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"The Agent class encapsulates LLM conversation state plus an optional vector-store and tools, acts as a message transformer, and by default provides three responder methods corresponding to LLM, Agent, and User.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8e3b75c74fb8d812792a7023149e3e7b5cff8f9663d6aa8bad5c08d4e7ebd56d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_261a81012f9db01fd2ce5c58697aa0974f279f69b452391379eace243bd45d46"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"LLM API responses can be cached via Redis or Momento (CACHE_TYPE=momento); if Redis settings are absent, Langroid falls back to a pure-Python in-memory cache via Fakeredis.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b13ffd944d0f7dc057cb755b8c52656adb56f47168a16b9f93cac31770e969a6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2c7bd3c93d3040660ad9208e02e173cb8b4b2ca7f2b083fe1110932aa9d81d63","slc_3deed355f0930270b81de163e5647fd616d42eb8d61242e47a0766a751aeddcd"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"Langroid requires Python 3.11+ and is installable from PyPI, with optional extras including hf-embeddings, doc-chat, db, postgres, and all (the latter increasing install size and startup time).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_be4165d8851873e314cff6b0f4875327711e4547bc9e5555bfee0b296c128b57","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f8ce40c27b9d796c2489152de85779aa7251075daa2e62206daf3d5a1d54757e"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"Langroid includes an MCP tool adapter that converts an MCP server's tools into Langroid ToolMessage instances so any LLM agent can leverage MCP servers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f6b6bb1b173887469c6bc272f026fd36266b6eb3c1e241aa55ca6297870462a3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"langroid/langroid@53c01d4e1a9e snapshot 15dd2d992e81e966","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_44f4100f9a4e8b8b53d9ddd56b164674fe8ff9b400ce6798b2eb2a7bc518988b"],"source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"text":"A Task wraps an Agent, manages iteration over the agent's responder methods, and orchestrates multi-agent interaction via hierarchical, recursive task delegation; sub-tasks are treated as additional responders used round-robin after the agent's own responders.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
